{"id":"mahabharata-7-097","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":97,"title":"सप्तनवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 97 · Satyaki's marvellous fight","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks how his shameless sons let Satyaki pass. Sanjaya describes how one man fought many, cutting off the arms of five hundred warriors who hurled huge stones, and then pressed on to Duhshasana's chariots.","kn":"ನಾಚಿಕೆಯಿಲ್ಲದ ತನ್ನ ಮಕ್ಕಳು ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ದಾಟಲು ಬಿಟ್ಟರೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಒಬ್ಬನೇ ಅನೇಕರೊಡನೆ ಹೋರಾಡಿ ದೊಡ್ಡ ಕಲ್ಲು ಎಸೆದ ಐನೂರು ವೀರರ ತೋಳು ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿದ್ದನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि उनके निर्लज्ज पुत्रों ने सात्यकि को कैसे निकलने दिया। संजय बताते हैं कि अकेले ने बहुतों से लड़कर बड़ी शिलाएँ फेंकने वाले पाँच सौ योद्धाओं की भुजाएँ काट दीं।","te":"సిగ్గులేని తన కొడుకులు సాత్యకిని ఎలా దాటనిచ్చారని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు. ఒక్కడే అనేకులతో పోరాడి పెద్ద బండలు విసిరిన ఐదు వందల వీరుల చేతులు నరికిన తీరును సంజయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"வெட்கமற்ற தன் மக்கள் சாத்யகியை எப்படிக் கடக்கவிட்டனர் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான். ஒருவனே பலருடன் போரிட்டுப் பெரும் பாறைகளை எறிந்த ஐந்நூறு வீரரின் கைகளை வெட்டியதைச் சஞ்சயன் விவரிக்கிறான்.","ml":"ലജ്ജയില്ലാത്ത തന്റെ പുത്രന്മാർ സാത്യകിയെ കടത്തിവിട്ടത് എങ്ങനെയെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ഒരാൾ പലരോടും പൊരുതി, വലിയ കല്ലുകൾ എറിഞ്ഞ അഞ്ഞൂറ് യോദ്ധാക്കളുടെ കൈകൾ വെട്ടിമാറ്റി, പിന്നെ ദുശ്ശാസനന്റെ രഥങ്ങളിലേക്ക് മുന്നേറി എന്ന് സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.97; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"संप्रमृद्य महत्सैन्यं यान्तं शैनेयमर्जुनम् ।\nनिर्ह्रीका मम ते पुत्राः किमकुर्वत संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Shaineya, after crushing that great army, went toward Arjuna, what did my shameless sons do, Sanjaya?"}},{"n":2,"text":"कथं चैषां तथा युद्धे धृतिरासीन्मुमूर्षताम् ।\nशैनेयचरितं दृष्ट्वा सदृशं सव्यसाचिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could their courage hold in that battle, when they were facing death, seeing Shaineya acting just like Savyasachin?"}},{"n":3,"text":"किं नु वक्ष्यन्ति ते क्षात्रं सैन्यमध्ये पराजिताः ।\nकथं च सात्यकिर्युद्धे व्यतिक्रान्तो महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What will they say to the kshatriya host, defeated in the midst of their army? How did the greatly renowned Satyaki get past them in the battle?"}},{"n":4,"text":"कथं च मम पुत्राणां जीवतां तत्र संजय ।\nशैनेयोऽभिययौ युद्धे तन्ममाचक्ष्व तत्त्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how, Sanjaya, with my sons still alive there, did Shaineya go on in the fight? Tell me truly."}},{"n":5,"text":"अत्यद्भुतमिदं तात त्वत्सकाशाच्छृणोम्यहम् ।\nएकस्य बहुभिर्युद्धं शत्रुभिर्वै महारथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is most marvelous, dear friend, what I hear from you: a battle of one against many enemy great chariot-warriors."}},{"n":6,"text":"विपरीतमहं मन्ये मन्दभाग्यान्सुतान्प्रति ।\nयत्रावध्यन्त समरे सात्वतेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think fate runs against my unlucky sons, that they were being struck down in battle by the great-souled Satvata."}},{"n":7,"text":"एकस्य हि न पर्याप्तं मत्सैन्यं तस्य संजय ।\nक्रुद्धस्य युयुधानस्य सर्वे तिष्ठन्तु पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My army, Sanjaya, was not enough for him alone, for the enraged Yuyudhana, never mind the Pandavas."}},{"n":8,"text":"निर्जित्य समरे द्रोणं कृतिनं युद्धदुर्मदम् ।\nयथा पशुगणान्सिंहस्तद्वद्धन्ता सुतान्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having beaten in battle Drona, the skilled, reckless fighter, he killed my sons as a lion kills herds of cattle."}},{"n":9,"text":"कृतवर्मादिभिः शूरैर्यत्तैर्बहुभिराहवे ।\nयुयुधानो न शकितो हन्तुं यः पुरुषर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yuyudhana, that bull among men, could not be killed by Kritavarman and many other heroes striving in the fight."}},{"n":10,"text":"नैतदीदृशकं युद्धं कृतवांस्तत्र फल्गुनः ।\nयादृशं कृतवान्युद्धं शिनेर्नप्ता महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Phalguna did not fight such a battle there as the greatly renowned grandson of Shini fought."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"तव दुर्मन्त्रिते राजन्दुर्योधनकृतेन च ।\nशृणुष्वावहितो भूत्वा यत्ते वक्ष्यामि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was through your bad counsel, O king, and through Duryodhana's doings. Listen carefully to what I shall tell you, Bharata."}},{"n":12,"text":"ते पुनः संन्यवर्तन्त कृत्वा संशप्तकान्मिथः ।\nपरां युद्धे मतिं कृत्वा पुत्रस्य तव शासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They turned back again, having pledged themselves among themselves like the Samshaptakas, setting their minds firmly on battle at your son's command."}},{"n":13,"text":"त्रीणि सादिसहस्राणि दुर्योधनपुरोगमाः ।\nशकाः काम्बोजबाह्लीका यवनाः पारदास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three thousand horsemen with Duryodhana in front, Shakas, Kambojas, Bahlikas, Yavanas, and Paradas,"}},{"n":14,"text":"कुणिन्दास्तङ्गणाम्बष्ठाः पैशाचाश्च समन्दराः ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्त शैनेयं शलभाः पावकं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kunindas, Tanganas, Ambashthas, Pishachas and Samandaras rushed at Shaineya, as moths rush at fire."}},{"n":15,"text":"युक्ताश्च पार्वतीयानां रथाः पाषाणयोधिनाम् ।\nशूराः पञ्चशता राजञ्शैनेयं समुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And five hundred brave chariots of mountaineers who fight with stones, harnessed, rushed at Shaineya, O king."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो रथसहस्रेण महारथशतेन च ।\nद्विरदानां सहस्रेण द्विसाहस्रैश्च वाजिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with a thousand chariots, a hundred great chariot-warriors, a thousand elephants, two thousand horses,"}},{"n":17,"text":"शरवर्षाणि मुञ्चन्तो विविधानि महारथाः ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्त शैनेयमसंख्येयाश्च पत्तयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those great chariot-warriors, releasing various kinds of arrow-showers, and countless foot soldiers, rushed at Shaineya."}},{"n":18,"text":"तांश्च संचोदयन्सर्वान्घ्नतैनमिति भारत ।\nदुःशासनो महाराज सात्यकिं पर्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urging them all, \"Kill him!\" Duhshasana, O Bharata, surrounded Satyaki."}},{"n":19,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम शैनेयचरितं महत् ।\nयदेको बहुभिः सार्धमसंभ्रान्तमयुध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a great and marvelous deed of Shaineya: that alone he fought many together, unflustered."}},{"n":20,"text":"अवधीच्च रथानीकं द्विरदानां च तद्बलम् ।\nसादिनश्चैव तान्सर्वान्दस्यूनपि च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He destroyed the chariot force, the elephants, the horsemen, and the dasyus, on every side."}},{"n":21,"text":"तत्र चक्रैर्विमथितैर्भग्नैश्च परमायुधैः ।\nअक्षैश्च बहुधा भग्नैरीषादण्डकबन्धुरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the earth was strewn with crushed wheels, broken great weapons, many broken axles, and with shafts and poles;"}},{"n":22,"text":"कूबरैर्मथितैश्चापि ध्वजैश्चापि निपातितैः ।\nवर्मभिश्चामरैश्चैव व्यवकीर्णा वसुंधरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With crushed yokes, fallen banners, armor and chowries."}},{"n":23,"text":"स्रग्भिराभरणैर्वस्त्रैरनुकर्षैश्च मारिष ।\nसंछन्ना वसुधा तत्र द्यौर्ग्रहैरिव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth there was covered, O lord, with garlands, ornaments, garments and chariot-floors, as the sky is with planets, O Bharata."}},{"n":24,"text":"गिरिरूपधराश्चापि पतिताः कुञ्जरोत्तमाः ।\nअञ्जनस्य कुले जाता वामनस्य च भारत ।\nसुप्रतीककुले जाता महापद्मकुले तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fallen excellent elephants, mountain-like, born of the Anjana line and of Vamana, and of the Supratika and Mahapadma lines, O Bharata,"}},{"n":25,"text":"ऐरावणकुले चैव तथान्येषु कुलेषु च ।\nजाता दन्तिवरा राजञ्शेरते बहवो हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And of the Airavata line and other lines, many fine elephants lay slain, O king."}},{"n":26,"text":"वनायुजान्पार्वतीयान्काम्बोजारट्टबाह्लिकान् ।\nतथा हयवरान्राजन्निजघ्ने तत्र सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Satyaki killed the Vanayu, mountain, Kamboja, Aratta and Bahlika horses, fine horses, O king."}},{"n":27,"text":"नानादेशसमुत्थांश्च नानाजात्यांश्च पत्तिनः ।\nनिजघ्ने तत्र शैनेयः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaineya killed foot soldiers of many lands and many kinds there by the hundred and by the thousand."}},{"n":28,"text":"तेषु प्रकाल्यमानेषु दस्यून्दुःशासनोऽब्रवीत् ।\nनिवर्तध्वमधर्मज्ञा युध्यध्वं किं सृतेन वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they were being driven off, Duhshasana said to the dasyus, \"Turn back, you who know no dharma! Fight! What good is running away?\""}},{"n":29,"text":"तांश्चापि सर्वान्संप्रेक्ष्य पुत्रो दुःशासनस्तव ।\nपाषाणयोधिनः शूरान्पार्वतीयानचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing all of them, your son Duhshasana urged on the brave mountaineers who fight with stones."}},{"n":30,"text":"अश्मयुद्धेषु कुशला नैतज्जानाति सात्यकिः ।\nअश्मयुद्धमजानन्तं घ्नतैनं युद्धकामुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are skilled in stone fighting; Satyaki does not know this. Kill that eager fighter who knows nothing of stone fighting."}},{"n":31,"text":"तथैव कुरवः सर्वे नाश्मयुद्धविशारदाः ।\nअभिद्रवत मा भैष्ट न वः प्राप्स्यति सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And all the Kurus too are not skilled in stone fighting. Rush at him and do not fear; Satyaki will not get through you.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"ततो गजशिशुप्रख्यैरुपलैः शैलवासिनः ।\nउद्यतैर्युयुधानस्य स्थिता मरणकाङ्क्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those mountain-dwellers, eager to die, stood with stones the size of elephant calves raised against Yuyudhana."}},{"n":33,"text":"क्षेपणीयैस्तथाप्यन्ये सात्वतस्य वधैषिणः ।\nचोदितास्तव पुत्रेण रुरुधुः सर्वतोदिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others too, urged by your son and wishing the Satvata's death, surrounded him on every side with hurled missiles."}},{"n":34,"text":"तेषामापततामेव शिलायुद्धं चिकीर्षताम् ।\nसात्यकिः प्रतिसंधाय त्रिंशतं प्राहिणोच्छरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they came on, wishing to fight with rocks, Satyaki aimed and shot thirty arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"तामश्मवृष्टिं तुमुलां पार्वतीयैः समीरिताम् ।\nबिभेदोरगसंकाशैर्नाराचैः शिनिपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bull of the Shinis split that tumultuous rain of stones sent by the mountaineers with iron arrows like serpents."}},{"n":36,"text":"तैरश्मचूर्णैर्दीप्यद्भिः खद्योतानामिव व्रजैः ।\nप्रायः सैन्यान्यवध्यन्त हाहाभूतानि मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those stones, ground to dust, glittering like swarms of fireflies, mostly struck the soldiers, who cried out in woe, O lord."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः पञ्चशताः शूराः समुद्यतमहाशिलाः ।\nनिकृत्तबाहवो राजन्निपेतुर्धरणीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then five hundred heroes, with great rocks raised, fell to the earth with their arms cut off, O king."}},{"n":38,"text":"पाषाणयोधिनः शूरान्यतमानानवस्थितान् ।\nअवधीद्बहुसाहस्रांस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He killed many thousands of the brave stone-fighters, who were striving and unmoving, and it seemed a marvel."}},{"n":39,"text":"ततः पुनर्बस्तमुखैरश्मवृष्टिं समन्ततः ।\nअयोहस्तैः शूलहस्तैर्दरदैः खशतङ्गणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then again a rain of stones came from all sides from goat-faced men, from iron-handed and spear-handed men, from Daradas, Khashas and Tanganas,"}},{"n":40,"text":"अम्बष्ठैश्च कुणिन्दैश्च क्षिप्तां क्षिप्तां स सात्यकिः ।\nनाराचैः प्रतिविव्याध प्रेक्षमाणो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Ambashthas and Kunindas; each time they hurled, that mighty Satyaki, watching, struck them back with iron arrows."}},{"n":41,"text":"अद्रीणां भिद्यमानानामन्तरिक्षे शितैः शरैः ।\nशब्देन प्राद्रवन्राजन्गजाश्वरथपत्तयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the rocks were split in the air by sharp arrows, with the noise elephants, horses, chariots and foot soldiers ran, O king."}},{"n":42,"text":"अश्मचूर्णैः समाकीर्णा मनुष्याश्च वयांसि च ।\nनाशक्नुवन्नवस्थातुं भ्रमरैरिव दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men and birds, covered with stone dust, could not stand, stung as if by bees."}},{"n":43,"text":"हतशिष्टा विरुधिरा भिन्नमस्तकपिण्डिकाः ।\nकुञ्जराः संन्यवर्तन्त युयुधानरथं प्रथि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The remaining elephants, bloodless, their head lumps split, turned toward Yuyudhana's chariot."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततः शब्दः समभवत्तव सैन्यस्य मारिष ।\nमाधवेनार्द्यमानस्य सागरस्येव दारुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a terrible roar rose from your army, my lord, tormented by the Madhava, like the roar of the sea."}},{"n":45,"text":"तं शब्दं तुमुलं श्रुत्वा द्रोणो यन्तारमब्रवीत् ।\nएष सूत रणे क्रुद्धः सात्वतानां महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that tumultuous noise, Drona said to his charioteer, \"That great chariot-warrior of the Satvatas, enraged in the battle, charioteer,"}},{"n":46,"text":"दारयन्बहुधा सैन्यं रणे चरति कालवत् ।\nयत्रैष शब्दस्तुमुलस्तत्र सूत रथं नय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is tearing the army apart in many ways and ranging in the fight like Death. Take the chariot where this tumultuous noise is."}},{"n":47,"text":"पाषाणयोधिभिर्नूनं युयुधानः समागतः ।\nतथा हि रथिनः सर्वे ह्रियन्ते विद्रुतैर्हयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely Yuyudhana has met the stone-fighters, for all the chariot-warriors are being carried off by bolting horses."}},{"n":48,"text":"विशस्त्रकवचा रुग्णास्तत्र तत्र पतन्ति च ।\nन शक्नुवन्ति यन्तारः संयन्तुं तुमुले हयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their weapons and armor gone, wounded, they fall here and there, and the charioteers cannot hold the horses in the confusion.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"इत्येवं ब्रुवतो राजन्भारद्वाजस्य धीमतः ।\nप्रत्युवाच ततो यन्ता द्रोणं शस्त्रभृतां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the wise son of Bharadvaja was speaking thus, O king, his charioteer replied to Drona, best of weapon-bearers."}},{"n":50,"text":"आयुष्मन्द्रवते सैन्यं कौरवेयं समन्ततः ।\nपश्य योधान्रणे भिन्नान्धावमानांस्ततस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Long-lived one, the Kaurava army is fleeing on every side; see the warriors broken in battle and running here and there."}},{"n":51,"text":"एते च सहिताः शूराः पाञ्चालाः पाण्डवैः सह ।\nत्वामेव हि जिघांसन्तः प्राद्रवन्ति समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And these brave Panchalas with the Pandavas, together, wishing to kill you alone, are rushing from all sides."}},{"n":52,"text":"अत्र कार्यं समाधत्स्व प्राप्तकालमरिंदम ।\nस्थाने वा गमने वापि दूरं यातश्च सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Settle what must be done here, tamer of foes; the time has come, to stand or to go, for Satyaki has gone far.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"तथैवं वदतस्तस्य भारद्वाजस्य मारिष ।\nप्रत्यदृश्यत शैनेयो निघ्नन्बहुविधान्रथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even as Bharadvaja's son was speaking, Shaineya was seen, killing chariots of many kinds."}},{"n":54,"text":"ते वध्यमानाः समरे युयुधानेन तावकाः ।\nयुयुधानरथं त्यक्त्वा द्रोणानीकाय दुद्रुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those men of yours, struck in battle by Yuyudhana, abandoned Yuyudhana's chariot and fled toward Drona's host."}},{"n":55,"text":"यैस्तु दुःशासनः सार्धं रथैः पूर्वं न्यवर्तत ।\nते भीतास्त्वभ्यधावन्त सर्वे द्रोणरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the chariots with which Duhshasana had earlier turned back, all of them, afraid, ran toward Drona's chariot."}}]}]}